{"date": "2026-11-04", "word": "Light", "summary": "A light day (forecast moderate). Thermals stayed light all day. The upslope ran from about 08:15 to about 16:45. The evening before, the page called it normal, about 4,400 ft, a hit. Midday the base averaged about 5,300 ft by the Kekoa camera, 900 ft higher than the evening's number; the morning update said about 4,900 ft, off by 400 ft. Most of the day the shear line was crossing Kula Highway near Omaopio; furthest north about 12:52, crossing Kula Highway near Kamehameha Schools; furthest south about 17:22, crossing Kula Highway at the middle Lower Kula Road junction. Data gaps: no readings all day from 2 stations (Kahikinui, Nakula); Upper Kahikinui stopped at 12:15; the Mesonet could not be reached on 20 of 51 updates.", "therm": "<strong>Light</strong> for the day, 10:00\u201314:00<div class=\"sub\">Kula Ag's measured air through the RRFS sounding (thermal.py); forecast was Moderate</div>", "base": "", "notes": ["Watched for: Summit spillover (P8) from 09:37.", "Camera against derived: morning about 900 ft higher, midday about 700 ft higher, afternoon about 400 ft higher."], "chart": "<div class=\"watch\"><div class=\"kind\">What the day did</div><ul><li>Watched for: Summit spillover (P8) from 09:37.</li><li>Camera against derived: morning about 900 ft higher, midday about 700 ft higher, afternoon about 400 ft higher.</li></ul></div><div style=\"font-weight:600;font-size:.9rem;margin:10px 0 2px\">Cloudbase</div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:14px;flex-wrap:wrap;font-size:.8rem;color:var(--muted,#6b6b66);margin:2px 0 4px\">\n<span><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:16px;border-top:2px dashed #8a5cd6;vertical-align:middle\"></span> Forecast (sounding)</span>\n<span><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:16px;height:2px;background:#2a78d6;vertical-align:middle\"></span> Derived (stations)</span><span><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:8px;height:8px;border-radius:50%;background:#3f9d5a;vertical-align: